ed:\n\n```\nthread 'run_returns_id_while_job_runs_then_it_finishes' panicked at tests/cli_e2e.rs:119:5:\n[\"--print\", \"--output-format\", \"stream-json\", \"--trust\", \"--approve-mcps\", \"--model\", \"composer-2.5\", \"--sandbox\", \"enabled\", \"--force\", \"--\", \"SLOW do it\", ...]\n```\n\nI restored `src/cli.rs` and the suite passes again.\n\nThe first swapped run reported a different line, `cli_e2e.rs:110`, with an `assertion left == right failed`. Line 110 is the `status == \"RUNNING\"` assert. The second swapped run didn't reproduce it. I don't know why it failed once. Six clean runs afterwards suggest a rare flake rather than a real regression. That assert is timing-sensitive: the fake agent sleeps 1s, so the record can already be terminal if `run` or the machine is slow.\n\n## Applied\n- **1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8:** done as written.\n  - The temp-file write now lives in one helper, `write_atomic`, in `src/status_record.rs`, used by both writers.\n  - The temp file is also removed if the rename fails.\n  - The old `FileStatusRecordWriter` temp name was `.<jobid>.<pid>.<ms>.tmp`; it is now `.<uuid>.tmp`.\n  - Both writers now use the new temp-file naming, which doesn't change what readers see.\n- **3:** the prompt file is created mode 0600 with `create_new`, and removed on three failure paths: the file write, the supervisor spawn, and the supervisor never writing its record.\n\n## Skipped\n- **6 (load only the config `run` needs):** it adds code, and I can't fix that inside the fence.\n  - The config-loading closure lives in `build_deps()` in `src/index.rs`, which is outside the fence.\n  - Loading just the config here would mean copying about 8 lines in `src/cli.rs`.\n  - `build_deps()` also still loads and validates `cli-config.json`, so a malformed file still makes `run` exit 1. Dropping that would change behaviour.\n\n## Friction\n- **Unused `cli_config`:** after item 2, `build_deps()` loads `cli_config` and nothing in the CLI uses it. The clean fix is a `load_config`-only helper in `index.rs` (outside the fence), which would also resolve item 6.\n- **Stale line numbers:** `cargo fmt` reflowed the test file between my edit and the run, so the failure line numbers and my string-replace patches went stale.\n- **No third bullet.**\n\nSTATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS","ttft_ms":5734,"type":"result","duration_ms":86580,"uuid":"46bd8e12-6fb0-471f-a233-1a62172c05a8","ttft_stream_ms":1785,"time_to_request_ms":398,"first_content_frame_ms":1785,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
